    "lawCode": "Add §1202-ii, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6190A\n\nSPONSOR: SKOUFIS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to authorizing the village of\nGoshen to impose a hotel and motel tax; and providing for the repeal of\nsuch provisions upon expiration thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nAuthorize the village of Goshen to impose a hotel and motel tax\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 - the tax shall not exceed five percent of the per diem rental\nrate for each room, and the tax shall not apply to any person occupying\na room for at least ninety consecutive days.\n\nSection 2 - The tax shall be collected and administered by the chief\nfiscal officer of the village of Goshen in the same manner as other\ntaxes are not collected\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation would allow the Village of Goshen to impose a hotel and\nmotel tax. The rate of such tax shall not exceed 5 percent of the per\ndiem rental rate for each room. Pursuant to the Municipal Home Rule Law,\na municipality may adopt local laws that relate to the levy and adminis-\ntration of local taxes if authorized by the State legislature. The\nvillage of Goshen has requested special legislation which will enable\nthem to collect a hotel and motel tax in an effort to raise additional\nrevenue for the village.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone for the state, increased revenue for the local government\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately and shall expire after two years\n",
